data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/final-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrocfw — final report\\n\\n## Mission\\nDeliver `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`, and\\n`tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string, with\\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exiting 0.\\n\\n## What happened\\n1. d001 (self-briefing) confirmed and closed.\\n2. Dispatched d002 to `dev`: implement `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`\\n   per the mission, verify locally, commit, reply truthfully.\\n3. `dev` replied with commit `968fc1f` on branch\\n   `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, reporting `python3 -m unittest\\n   discover -s tests` exits 0 with 2 tests passing.\\n\\n## Independent verification (not just trusting the report)\\n- `cs-campaign-member fetch dev` confirmed the branch tree differs from base\\n  with real changes.\\n- Diffed `refs/remotes/campaign/dev/subject` against base commit\\n  `1fdce0c05b0104010437749bc427c96cf007bd0b`:\\n  - `src/greet.py` adds `greet(name)` returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n  - `tests/test_greet.py` adds unittest cases for `greet(\\\"World\\\")` and\\n    `greet(\\\"\\\")`.\\n- Checked out the branch in an isolated worktree (`/tmp/verify_subject`) and\\n  ran `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself:\\n  ```\\n  ..\\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------------\\n  Ran 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\n  OK\\n  ```\\n  Exit code: 0.\\n- Worktree removed after verification.\\n\\n## Judgment\\nAll three mission criteria are satisfied and independently confirmed:\\n- `src/greet.py` with `greet(name)` → `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` — present and correct.\\n- `tests/test_greet.py` covering a normal name and the empty string — present\\n  and correct.\\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 — confirmed by running it\\n  myself against the fetched branch, not just by reading dev's report.\\n\\n`dev`'s d002 work was accepted (`cs-campaign-member accept dev`).\\n\\n## Outcome\\ncampaign-met — every stated criterion is satisfied; nothing remains unmet.\\n\\n## Note on orchestrator's own branch\\nPer role (`orchestrator.md`: \\\"you run this campaign and judge it; you write\\nno code yourself\\\"), no code was written on\\n`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`; the delivered work lives\\non `dev`'s branch, `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit\\n`968fc1f`.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

